 += p_transform.basis.xform(p_eye_offsets[v]);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp","commit_id":"bef0b981b1099dabe388cc98ecc24992cede0f54","original_commit_id":"bef0b981b1099dabe388cc98ecc24992cede0f54","user":{"login":"williamdev06","id":135645566,"node_id":"U_kgDOCBXJfg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/135645566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06","html_url":"https://github.com/williamdev06","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/williamdev06/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"You are right that the p_transform doesn't have the eye offset baked in, the main pass keeps the view matrix at the head and puts the per-eye separation in the projection, as far as I can tell. The reprojection does need the eye offset so it can match where the last frame's color was sampled for each eye, so I add the offset into the transform here, there might be a better way of adding the offset that I am unaware of. I checked whether it's actually doing anything: at normal scale the difference is sub-IPD and only shows under head motion, so it's easy to miss. But exaggerating the offset (×15) clearly breaks the reflection, so at least from what I can tell it is needed.","created_at":"2026-06-15T17:56:29Z","updated_at":"2026-06-15T17:56:30Z","h